(O/'FINAL_SUPPLEMENTARY_FIGURE_LEGENDS_PHASE12.md').write_text('''# Supplementary figure legends\n\n## Supplementary Figure S1 | Subtype annotation provenance and donor representation\na, Original-author canine T-cell labels versus frozen Level2 labels. b, Canine coverage under the frozen >=20-cell and >=3-healthy/3-CIE-dog gate. c, Human representation in the recovered 13-healthy/6-active-Crohn subset under >=20 cells in >=5 participants per group. d, Recovery within the frozen 21,378-cell broad-T universe: 15,670 valid author fine labels comprised 15,233 T-related and 437 NK/ILC identities. Missing labels indicate unavailable provenance, not biological absence.\n\n## Supplementary Figure S2 | Subtype-resolved disease-associated programs\nSigned NES values are shown for canine and human T-cell, epithelial and myeloid states. All six panels use one recomputed global symmetric Signed NES scale (-3.1 to +3.1), rounded from the largest absolute plotted value. Black outlines indicate within-species BH q < 0.05: dog T 9/15, human T 7/18, dog epithelial 8/12, eligibility-corrected human epithelial 11/12, dog myeloid 2/3 and human Macrophage 0/3. Formal human models included only participant-state pseudobulks with at least 20 cells: Early Enterocyte 11 healthy/6 Crohn, Enterocyte 13/6, Ileum Goblet 13/6, TA 8/5 and Macrophage 13/6. Species-native enrichment is shown separately; strict shared-ortholog subtype enrichment was not demonstrated.\n\n## Supplementary Figure S3 | Donor robustness and participant-selection sensitivity\na, Valid leave-one-CIE-dog-out Goblet estimates. b, Valid participant-omission estimates for Human Ileum Goblet and CD103+ CD4 respiratory programs; HA49 marks the prespecified T-cell sensitivity signal. Human Goblet mitochondrial-respiration and oxidative-phosphorylation directions were retained in all 19 valid omissions. c, Human myeloid programs across the original 27-participant cohort, recovered 19-participant broad lineage and recovered author-labelled subset. Recovered broad-myeloid estimates retained the positive primary directions. d, Native-species macrophage NES. None of the three Human Macrophage programs passed the three-test BH family. LODO is not independent replication, and separately ranked native-species effects do not establish conserved or species-specific macrophage mechanisms.\n\n## Supplementary Figure S4 | Selection-aware matched-background calibration\na, Exactly 5,000 saved K20 draws. Observed concordance was 18/23 (78.26%) versus a 63.78% background mean; 360 draws were at least as large, giving the plus-one conditional upper-tail frequency 0.0722. b, Frozen K10/K20/K30 sensitivity. c, Excluding all five match-limited units gave 14/18 = 77.78%, background 65.33% and tail 0.1706. This exclusion is diagnostic and does not replace the 23-unit primary analysis; no participant-label permutation P value was estimated.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
print(out);print('CHANGES',len(changes))


